+
+# Rental service period, pricing and booking rules
+
+## Context
+The school's rules fix money (integer cents), UTC times, whole-day periods and no overlaps, but leave
+some details open.
+
+## Decision
+- A period is half-open `[start, end)`; `end` is the start of the day after the last day, so a booking
+  ending on a day can be followed by one starting that day.
+- Only ISO-8601 strings with a `Z` suffix at exactly midnight are accepted; offsets and date-only
+  strings are rejected rather than converted. Returned `start`/`end` are normalised to `toISOString()`.
+- `end` must be strictly after `start`.
+- Equipment ids are unique and `dailyPrice` must be a non-negative integer; invalid items throw.
+- Booking ids are a sequential counter (`booking-N`), keeping the service deterministic (no clock or
+  randomness).
+
+## Consequences
+Behaviour is strict and predictable. Cancellations will need to keep bookings addressable by id and
+compare the start with the cancellation time (24 hours rule), which this design allows.
